<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Boris Yeltsin is elected president and resists the August coup</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The republic is renamed the Russian Federation on 25 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Soviet troops kill fourteen civilians at the Vilnius television tower</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence is restored on 20 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Full independence is restored on 21 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/soviet-union"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Soviet%20Union.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Soviet Union</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union is dissolved on 26 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-india"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20India.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of India</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Economic liberalisation begins after a balance-of-payments crisis</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Somaliland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Somaliland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence is declared at Burao on 18 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-colombia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Colombia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Colombia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution replaces the charter of 1886</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/federation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union, a federation of fifteen union republics, is dissolved</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hungary"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hungary.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hungary</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The removal of state subsidies and rapid privatisation, with the Yugoslav Wars on the southern border, bring a severe recession.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 15 March Germany regains its full sovereignty from the Allies.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/azerbaijan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Azerbaijan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Azerbaijan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Council of Azerbaijan adopts a Declaration of Independence on 18 October, affirmed by a nationwide referendum in December.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/armenia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Armenia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Armenia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Armenia declares its statehood on 21 September after the failed August coup in Moscow; Levon Ter-Petrosyan is elected the first president in October.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/georgia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Georgia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Georgia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Council declares independence on 9 April after the referendum of 31 March; Zviad Gamsakhurdia is elected president on 26 May with 86.5 percent.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uzbekistan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uzbekistan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uzbekistan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Uzbekistan declares independence on 31 August after the failed coup in Moscow; Islam Karimov is elected president on 29 December.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-morocco"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Morocco.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Morocco</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A UN-monitored ceasefire ends fifteen years of war with the Polisario Front in Western Sahara, leaving the territory's status undecided.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/east-timor"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/East%20Timor.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>East Timor</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Indonesian military massacres more than 200 demonstrators, a turning point that brings international pressure on Indonesia.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union is dissolved, after the Revolutions of 1989 across Eastern Europe</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/communism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Communism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Communism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union is dissolved, after the Revolutions of 1989 have brought down most of the Eastern Bloc</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/borobudur"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Borobudur.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Borobudur</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UNESCO lists the Borobudur Temple Compounds as a World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ukrainian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ukrainian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ukrainian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Soviet adopted the Act of Declaration of Independence of Ukraine, ending the Ukrainian SSR</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Facsimile Edition and the opening of the Huntington Library's photographs ended restricted access</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/armenian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Armenian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Armenian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Armenia confirms its independence by referendum on 21 September, and the Armenian SSR ceases to exist with the dissolution of the Soviet Union on 26 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kyiv"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kyiv.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kyiv</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ukraine declares independence in Kyiv, which becomes the capital of an independent state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/saint-petersburg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saint%20Petersburg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saint Petersburg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum restores the name Saint Petersburg</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/benin-city"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Benin%20City.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Benin City</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Benin City becomes the capital of the new Edo State</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/addis-ababa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Addis%20Ababa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Addis Ababa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ethiopian People's Revolutionary Democratic Front seizes the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/gondar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gondar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gondar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Forces of the EPRDF occupy Gondar in May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/tomb-of-tutankhamun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tomb%20of%20Tutankhamun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tomb of Tutankhamun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A rainstorm flooded the tomb through a fault in the burial chamber ceiling</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/romance-of-the-three-kingdoms"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Romance%20of%20the%20Three%20Kingdoms.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Romance of the Three Kingdoms</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Moss Roberts publishes a full English translation with maps, a list of characters and notes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet Union dissolves, and its constituent nations abandon Marxist–Leninist models</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism-leninism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism%E2%80%93Leninism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism–Leninism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gorbachev announces the dissolution of the Soviet Union on 25 December</span></li></ul></section>
